<p>Donors meeting in Berlin pledged about €1.3 billion in new aid for Sudan as the war that began on 2023-04-15 entered its fourth year. The conference focused on helping relief agencies sustain urgent operations as fighting keeps driving hunger, displacement, and severe shortages across the country. The new commitments give humanitarian groups fresh support at a time when needs remain immense and the chances of a negotiated end to the conflict still appear remote.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/7Ki7CAvSKitCTLUDDcs_bj-_YwZXNMWRNR0Ckj1n6a-eilxRF5CKcydezN5VnP54Sm5RCNN7XIIVHBjR4VlOQIz_dD8YzLzwra9P7EG9wAknZKkBa6kWkmXf1GuJ_mXULYQnouXylo6Mfp2otS34s7HveN5Cs1VVuwUYcgp-fgNuYVhGXnXHtcDLByY' alt='A 2-month-old patient, Saidal Altaher, receives treatment for malnutrition in Port Sudan, Sudan.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Funding target beaten: The Guardian reported that donors exceeded the goal organizers set for the Berlin conference, giving Sudan relief efforts more than planners initially sought.</li><li>Indirect peace track: Al Jazeera reported that participants also discussed ways to move ceasefire negotiations forward, even though the Berlin gathering itself focused on aid pledging.</li><li>Middle East effect: The New York Times reported that Sudan’s hunger emergency is worsening because disruption linked to conflict in the Middle East is adding pressure to already strained aid flows.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Germany and co-hosts: Organizers treated Berlin as a practical push to fund urgent aid projects while broader diplomacy remained stuck, reflecting how few options are currently available to ease civilian suffering. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/germany-sudan-aid-conference-in-berlin-raises-%E2%82%AC1-3b/a-76786563'>DW</a>, <a href='https://www.dw.com/en/berlin-hosts-sudan-conference-amid-brutal-forgotten-war/a-76798246'>DW</a>)</li><li>Sudanese civilian figures: Some Sudanese political and civilian participants focused on representation itself, with disagreements over which civilian voices should speak for the country in international diplomacy. (<a href='https://allafrica.com/stories/202604150696.html'>AllAfrica</a>)</li><li>UN leadership: António Guterres used the donor conference to argue that relief pledges alone are not enough, pairing warnings about hunger with a broader call for the war to stop. (<a href='https://www.channelafrica.co.za/channelafrica/news/the-nightmare-must-end-guteress-asks-after-over-1-billion-pledged-for-sudan/'>Channel Africa</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/berlin-hosts-sudan-conference-amid-brutal-forgotten-war/a-76798246'>Berlin hosts Sudan conference amid brutal, forgotten war</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2026/apr/15/more-than-1bn-pledged-for-sudan-as-humanitarian-crisis-deepens'>More than £1bn pledged for Sudan as humanitarian crisis deepens</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/15/world/africa/sudan-war-hunger-crisis.html'>Sudan Enters Fourth Year of War Amid World’s Most Severe Humanitarian Crisis</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://allafrica.com/stories/202604150696.html'>Sudan: &#x27;Presence Vs Absence&#x27; At Berlin Conference, Disputes Over Civilian Representation, and Exclusion of Warring Parties</a> - allafrica.com</li><li><a href='https://www.channelafrica.co.za/channelafrica/news/the-nightmare-must-end-guteress-asks-after-over-1-billion-pledged-for-sudan/'>Foreign ministers at the Third International Conference for Sudan in Berlin that is hosted by Germany, the African Union, the European Union, France and the United Kingdom, pledges $1 billion in assistance to Sudan as the war entered its fourth year and the country faces a hunger crisis.</a> - channelafrica.co.za</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/15/countries-pledge-1-5bn-for-sudan-crisis-as-war-enters-fourth-year'>Donors pledge €1.3 billion (US$1.5 billion) in foreign aid for Sudan at an international conference in Berlin, Germany, marking the third anniversary of the beginning of Sudan&#x27;s civil war, as participants also discuss efforts to advance ceasefire negotiations.</a> - aljazeera.com</li></ul>